HIERARCHY:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Oracle Database
│
├── Tablespace (Logical Storage Container)
│   │
│   ├── Datafile 1 (.dbf)
│   ├── Datafile 2 (.dbf)
│   └── Datafile 3 (.dbf)
│
│      ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│      │     Segments                │
│      └─────────────────────────────┘
│                   │
│                   ├── Table Segment
│                   ├── Index Segment
│                   ├── Undo Segment
│                   └── Temporary Segment
│
│                   │
│                   ▼
│      ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│      │        Extents              │
│      └─────────────────────────────┘
│
│                   │
│                   ├── Extent 1
│                   ├── Extent 2
│                   ├── Extent 3
│                   └── ...
│
│                   │
│                   ▼
│      ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│      │         Blocks              │
│      └─────────────────────────────┘
│
│                   │
│                   ├── Block 1
│                   ├── Block 2
│                   ├── Block 3
│                   └── ...
│
└── Other Tablespaces
    ├── SYSTEM
            └── Knows EMPLOYEES table exists
    ├── SYSAUX
            └── Stores monitoring information
    ├── USERS
            └── EMPLOYEES table data
    ├── UNDOTBS1
            └── Stores old salary value (10000)
    └── TEMP
            └── May be used if operation requires sorting
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIMPLE DEFINITIONS:
==================
when a user creates and updates a table:
---------------------------------------
SYSTEM   → knows the table exists
SYSAUX   → records performance history
USERS    → stores actual rows
UNDOTBS1 → stores old copies of rows
TEMP     → helps with temporary calculations

ANALOGY:
=======
SYSTEM   = Oracle's Brain
SYSAUX   = Brain's Assistant
USERS    = Business/User Data
UNDOTBS1 = Time Machine (old values)
TEMP     = Scratch Pad / Rough Work Area
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key difference between system and sysaux:
==========================================
SYSTEM = Mandatory for Oracle to run
SYSAUX = Helper tablespace that offloads extra Oracle components from SYSTEM

# COMPARISON TABLE
=========================================================================================
Feature	                          SYSTEM	                   SYSAUX
=========================================================================================
Purpose	                       Core Oracle metadata	      Auxiliary metadata
Mandatory	                        Yes	                         Yes
Contains	                    Data Dictionary	          Additional Oracle components
Importance	                     Most critical	           Important but supporting
Created During DB Creation	        Yes	                         Yes
Can Oracle Run Without It?	         No	                          No
Stores User Tables?	            Never recommended	       Never recommended
=========================================================================================

